  "note": "Election of the Carrickfergus Borough Council, nominations received Friday 5 January 1923; nine candidates for the council and no contest (Northern Whig, 13 January 1923, p. 6). The paper prints: 'only nine candidates have been nominated for the 18 seats, and consequently no contest will take place. All were retiring members with the exception of Mr. William Henry Elliott.' The nine returned are recorded here; the council's remaining seats were not part of this return. Returned unopposed."
